wb-node-red (0.2.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Static service (docs/adr/0003): the base docker-compose.yml now hardcodes
    the loopback port (127.0.0.1:21880 -> 1880) instead of relying on runtime
    port allocation.
  * Image is now a byte-for-byte MIRROR of vanilla nodered/node-red:4.0.2 (no
    derived -wb1 build, no Dockerfile). The WB palette node-red-contrib-wirenboard
    (pure JS) is npm-vendored into the .deb at build time and refreshed into
    /data/node_modules at install, so the editor has the WB nodes out of the box
    with no runtime npm (docs/adr/0006). Build now needs nodejs + npm.
  * Ships its own standalone nginx server block at
    /etc/nginx/sites-available/node-red.conf (symlinked into sites-enabled/),
    reusing the homeui login via auth_request, instead of generating it
    (docs/adr/0005).
  * postinst provisions the broker bridge it needs (wb-docker-app
    provision-mqtt) before installing — the helper no longer does this at its
    own install (docs/adr/0004).
  * postinst passes --data-uid 1000 (Node-RED's container user) so the helper
    chowns the seeded /data; the nginx site is now enabled by the helper with an
    absolute-target symlink. Dropped the relative dh_link .links file, which
    broke on WB's bind-mounted sites-enabled. Both controller-validated.
  * New postrm reloads nginx via wb-docker-app reload-proxy after dpkg removes
    the static drop-in, so removal does not leave a stale server-block proxying
    to a dead upstream.

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0300

wb-node-red (0.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: base docker-compose.yml with wb.* labels installed to
    /usr/lib/wb-docker-app/node-red/; thin postinst/prerm calling into
    wb-docker-app (issue #1, walking skeleton).

 -- Wiren Board Team <info@wirenboard.com>  Tue, 02 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
